module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AffineBlowup.ChartEquiv
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Defs

/-!
# The models of the affine blowup algebra agree

The affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]` of [Stacks, Tag 052Q] is realized five times in this
development, and a result proved over one realization says nothing about another until they are
identified. This module identifies them.

Four of the five are `R`-subalgebras of `Localization.Away a`, differing only in how the
subalgebra is cut out:

* `affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a)` (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Defs`), the
  subalgebra *generated* by the fractions `y/a` with `y ∈ I`. This is the form
  `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpAffineChartRing`, the chart of `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, is built
  from.
* `affineBlowupAlgebraAway I a` (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Basic`), the same generated
  subalgebra written with `IsLocalization.Away.invSelf`.
* `Stacks.AffineBlowup.affineBlowupAlgebra I a ha`
  (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AffineBlowup.Valuation`), the subalgebra given by the explicit
  carrier `{y | ∃ n x, x ∈ Iⁿ ∧ y · aⁿ = x}`.
* `affineBlowup I a` (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Basic`), the subalgebra generated by the
  same fractions written as `Localization.mk`. This is the ring whose spectrum
  `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` identifies with an affine open of the blowup, so it is the
  realization a ring-level statement has to reach to be read on a chart.

The last is the quotient model `Blowup I a` (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Basic`), the
fractions `x/aⁿ` with `x ∈ Iⁿ` modulo the `a`-power-torsion relation. It is the form the
ring-level strict transform (`strictTransform`, [Stacks, Tag 053H]) and the ring-level
flattening results of [Stacks, Tag 0810] are stated over, and it is already identified with the
third realization by `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra`.

What was missing, and is supplied here, is the link from that chain to the two *generated*
realizations — the ones the scheme-level charts are built from. With it, a ring-level statement
about `Blowup I a` can be read on a blowup chart of a scheme, in either chart construction.

## Main results

* `affineBlowupAlgebraAway_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra`: the two generated realizations agree.
* `Stacks.AffineBlowup.affineBlowupAlgebra_eq_affineBlowupAlgebraAway`: the explicit carrier is
  the generated subalgebra, for `a ∈ I`.
* `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization`: **the quotient model is the
  subalgebra the scheme charts use**, `Blowup I a ≃ₐ[R] affineBlowupAlgebra I a
  (Localization.Away a)`.
* `affineBlowup_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra`: a fifth spelling, `affineBlowup I a`, is the same
  subalgebra written with `Localization.mk`; this is the one the scheme charts are the spectra of.
* `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowup`: the quotient model is that fifth spelling.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis `a ∈ I` is needed only for the explicit-carrier realization: without it the
carrier is still a subalgebra, but not the generated one — the generators `y/a` have `y ∈ I`,
while membership of the carrier only asks for *some* power. The two generated realizations agree
with no hypothesis at all, since `IsLocalization.mk' S y ⟨a, _⟩` and
`IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a * algebraMap R S y` are the same element of the localization.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 053H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0810](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0810)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- **The two generated realizations of the affine blowup algebra agree.** Both are the
`R`-subalgebra of `Localization.Away a` generated by the fractions `y/a` with `y ∈ I`; one writes
the fraction as `IsLocalization.mk'`, the other as a multiple of
`IsLocalization.Away.invSelf`. No hypothesis on `a` is needed. -/
theorem affineBlowupAlgebraAway_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra (I : Ideal R) (a : R) :
    affineBlowupAlgebraAway I a = affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a) := by
  unfold affineBlowupAlgebra affineBlowupAlgebraAway
  congr 1
  ext z
  constructor <;> rintro ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ <;> refine ⟨y, hy, ?_⟩ <;>
    rw [IsLocalization.mk'_eq_mul_mk'_one] <;> simp [IsLocalization.Away.invSelf, mul_comm]

/-- **The `Localization.mk` realization of the affine blowup algebra is the generated one.**
`affineBlowup I a` (`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Basic`) is the `R`-subalgebra of
`Localization.Away a` generated by the fractions `Localization.mk y ⟨a, _⟩` with `y ∈ I`; it is
`affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a)` with the fraction written as a
`Localization.mk` rather than an `IsLocalization.mk'`, and the two agree by
`Localization.mk_eq_mk'`. No hypothesis on `a` is needed.

This is the realization the affine charts of the blowup of a *scheme* are the spectra of
(`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart`), so it is what a ring-level statement about `Blowup I a` has
to be transported along to be read on a chart. -/
theorem affineBlowup_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra (I : Ideal R) (a : R) :
    affineBlowup I a = affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a) := by
  unfold affineBlowup affineBlowupAlgebra affineBlowupGenSet
  congr 1
  ext z
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_image]
  constructor <;> rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ <;> exact ⟨x, hx, by rw [Localization.mk_eq_mk']⟩

namespace Stacks.AffineBlowup

/-- **The explicit-carrier realization of the affine blowup algebra is the generated one.** An
element `y` of `Localization.Away a` satisfies `y · aⁿ = x` for some `x ∈ Iⁿ` exactly when it is
`(1/a)ⁿ · x` for such an `x`, because `a` is invertible in the localization; and for `a ∈ I` the
latter description is the generated subalgebra, by `mem_affineBlowup_iff`. -/
theorem affineBlowupAlgebra_eq_affineBlowupAlgebraAway (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (ha : a ∈ I) :
    affineBlowupAlgebra I a ha = _root_.affineBlowupAlgebraAway I a := by
  refine SetLike.ext fun z ↦ ?_
  have key (n : ℕ) (y : Localization.Away a) :
      z * algebraMap R _ a ^ n = y ↔ z = IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ n * y := by
    have h := invSelf_pow_mul_algebraMap_pow a n
    constructor <;> intro hz
    · linear_combination (-z) * h + IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ n * hz
    · linear_combination algebraMap R _ a ^ n * hz + y * h
  simp only [mem_affineBlowupAlgebra ha, mem_affineBlowup_iff I a ha, key]

/-- **The quotient model of the affine blowup algebra is the subalgebra the scheme charts use.**
The quotient model `Blowup I a` — over which the ring-level strict transform ([Stacks, Tag 053H])
and the ring-level flattening theorem ([Stacks, Tag 0810]) are stated — is isomorphic as an
`R`-algebra to `affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a)`, which is what both scheme-chart
constructions of the blowup are built from.

This is `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra` followed by the identification of
the explicit-carrier realization with the generated one. -/
def blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization {I : Ideal R} {a : R} [ha : Fact (a ∈ I)] :
    Blowup I a ≃ₐ[R] _root_.affineBlowupAlgebra I a (Localization.Away a) :=
  blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra.trans <| Subalgebra.equivOfEq _ _ <|
    (affineBlowupAlgebra_eq_affineBlowupAlgebraAway I a ha.out).trans
      (affineBlowupAlgebraAway_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra I a)

/-- The isomorphism onto the subalgebra the scheme charts use is the comparison map: its value at
`x`, viewed in `Localization.Away a`, is `blowupToAway x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization_coe {I : Ideal R} {a : R} [ha : Fact (a ∈ I)]
    (x : Blowup I a) :
    (blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization (I := I) (a := a) x : Localization.Away a)
      = blowupToAway x :=
  blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra_coe x

/-- **The quotient model is the realization the scheme charts are the spectra of.** The quotient
model `Blowup I a` — over which the ring-level strict transform ([Stacks, Tag 053H]) and the
ring-level flattening theorem ([Stacks, Tag 0810]) are stated — is isomorphic as an `R`-algebra
to `affineBlowup I a`, which is the ring whose spectrum
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` identifies with an affine open of the blowup.

This is `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization` followed by
`affineBlowup_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra`. -/
def blowupEquivAffineBlowup {I : Ideal R} {a : R} [Fact (a ∈ I)] :
    Blowup I a ≃ₐ[R] _root_.affineBlowup I a :=
  blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization.trans <| Subalgebra.equivOfEq _ _ <|
    (affineBlowup_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra I a).symm

/-- The isomorphism onto the chart realization is the comparison map: its value at `x`, viewed in
`Localization.Away a`, is `blowupToAway x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem blowupEquivAffineBlowup_coe {I : Ideal R} {a : R} [Fact (a ∈ I)] (x : Blowup I a) :
    (blowupEquivAffineBlowup (I := I) (a := a) x : Localization.Away a) = blowupToAway x :=
  blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebraLocalization_coe x

end Stacks.AffineBlowup

end
